{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Edward Khantzian is a professor of psychiatry, part time at Harvard Medical School.","title":"Edward Khantzian"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is the originator of the self-medication hypothesis of drug abuse, which states that individuals use drugs in an attempt to self-medicate states of distress and suffering.","title":"Edward Khantzian"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Richard Yardumian (Armenian: Ռիչարդ Յարդումյան , April 5, 1917 – August 15, 1985) was an Armenian-American classical music composer.","title":"Richard Yardumian"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"A General Theory of Love is a book about the science of human emotions and biological psychiatry written by Thomas Lewis, Fari Amini and Richard Lannon, psychiatry professors at the University of California, San Francisco, and first published by Random House in 2000.","title":"A General Theory of Love"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It has since been reissued twice, with new editions appearing in 2001 and 2007.","title":"A General Theory of Love"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"PHMI was founded in 1994 as a subsidiary of Harvard University.","title":"Partners Harvard Medical International"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" From 1994 until 2008, the organization was known as Harvard Medical International, or HMI.","title":"Partners Harvard Medical International"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Operated as a division of Harvard Medical School, HMI’s original focus was to work with institutions around the world – primarily medical schools and health care delivery organizations – interested in developing education programs and health care programs with the help of Harvard professors and the staff of Harvard Medical School.","title":"Partners Harvard Medical International"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In April 2008, HMI became Partners Harvard Medical International and became part of Partners HealthCare.","title":"Partners Harvard Medical International"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Since 1994, the company has developed collaborative relationships with institutions in more than 40 countries.","title":"Partners Harvard Medical International"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Elissa Panush Benedek (born September 28, 1936) is an American psychiatrist specializing in child and adolescent psychiatry and forensic psychiatry.","title":"Elissa P. Benedek"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is an adjunct clinical professor of psychiatry at the University of Michigan Medical Center.","title":"Elissa P. Benedek"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She served as director of research and training at the Center for Forensic Psychiatry in Ann Arbor for 25 years and was president of the American Psychiatric Association from 1990 to 1991.","title":"Elissa P. Benedek"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" She is regarded as an expert on child abuse and trauma, and has testified in high-profile court cases.","title":"Elissa P. Benedek"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" She also focuses on ethics, psychiatric aspects of disasters and terrorism, and domestic violence.","title":"Elissa P. Benedek"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In addition to her own books, book chapters, and articles, she has collaborated with her husband, attorney Richard S. Benedek, on studies of divorce, child custody, and child abuse.","title":"Elissa P. Benedek"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Armand M. Nicholi, M.D., Jr. is a clinical professor of psychiatry at Harvard Medical School and the Massachusetts General Hospital.","title":"Armand Nicholi"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His clinical work and research has focused on the impact of absent parents on the emotional development of children and young adults.","title":"Armand Nicholi"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He is the editor and coauthor of the classic "The Harvard Guide to Psychiatry" (3rd edition, 1999).","title":"Armand Nicholi"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He was also a founding board member of the Family Research Council.","title":"Armand Nicholi"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: no
